{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 183 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "401ee6bb8443e8f7fbcbca00e79e0f463e2c03b56aa7fc50e24162af0d5d6517" :edb/db-before-t 182 :edb/db-after-t 183 :edb/tx-data [[13194139533495 50 #inst "2026-10-11T02:48:29.489Z" 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186054823 1038 #edb/ref 17592186404141 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186059697 1038 #edb/ref 17592186404210 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186059697 1038 #edb/ref 17592186404217 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186060420 1068 #edb/ref 17592186059112 13194139533495 17592186045585 false] [17592186060420 1068 #edb/ref 17592186404204 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186060420 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186060420 1071 "Find the contrapositive of the following statement:\n\n**If** it is not warm outside, **then** you need a jacket." 13194139533495 17592186045585 false] [17592186060420 1071 "Find the contrapositive of the following statement: \n\n$\\,$ **If** it is not warm outside, **then** you need a jacket." 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186060420 1074 "In our conditional statement: \n\n- The antecedent is $A:$ It is not warm outside.\n\n- The consequent is $B:$ You need a jacket.\n\nThe contrapositive of a conditional statement $A⇒B$ is given by \n\n$$\n¬B⇒¬A.\n$$\n\nFirst, we write down the negations of $A$ and $B:$\n\n- $¬A:$ It is warm outside.\n\n- $¬B:$ You don't need a jacket.\n\nTherefore, the contrapositive is the following: \n\n$\\,$ If you don't need a jacket, then it is warm outside." 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186087793 1038 #edb/ref 17592186404190 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186087796 1038 #edb/ref 17592186404251 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186087842 1038 #edb/ref 17592186404300 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186087842 1038 #edb/ref 17592186404307 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186087859 1038 #edb/ref 17592186404148 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186087872 1038 #edb/ref 17592186404265 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186087894 1038 #edb/ref 17592186404272 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186096734 1038 #edb/ref 17592186404391 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186100900 1038 #edb/ref 17592186404237 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186105771 1038 #edb/ref 17592186404176 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186115208 1038 #edb/ref 17592186404197 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186124454 1038 #edb/ref 17592186404127 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186124529 1038 #edb/ref 17592186404134 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186124529 1038 #edb/ref 17592186404384 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186124537 1038 #edb/ref 17592186404155 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186124538 1038 #edb/ref 17592186404279 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186124538 1038 #edb/ref 17592186404314 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186124552 1038 #edb/ref 17592186404183 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186124584 1038 #edb/ref 17592186404286 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186124584 1038 #edb/ref 17592186404293 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186124607 1038 #edb/ref 17592186404120 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186124662 1038 #edb/ref 17592186404356 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186124662 1038 #edb/ref 17592186404377 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186124663 1038 #edb/ref 17592186404370 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186124664 1038 #edb/ref 17592186404258 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186124664 1038 #edb/ref 17592186404363 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186129088 1038 #edb/ref 17592186404321 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186129089 1038 #edb/ref 17592186404328 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186157247 1038 #edb/ref 17592186404230 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186157828 1068 #edb/ref 17592186155859 13194139533495 17592186045585 false] [17592186157828 1068 #edb/ref 17592186404224 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186157828 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186157828 1074 "First, we simplify the phrase \"the pen is blue and it is a blue pen\" to just \"the pen is blue.\" The sentence now reads\n\n\"The pen is blue, or the pen is blue or it is a red pen.\"\n\nThen, using the associative law, we can move the comma in the sentence:\n\n\"The pen is blue or the pen is blue, or it is a red pen.\"\n\nNow, we simplify the phrase \"the pen is blue or the pen is blue\" to just \"the pen is blue.\" The sentence now reads\n\n\"The pen is blue, or it is a red pen.\"\n\nFinally, we simplify the sentence to\n\n\"The pen is blue or red.\"" 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186184198 1038 #edb/ref 17592186404335 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186184198 1038 #edb/ref 17592186404342 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186184198 1038 #edb/ref 17592186404349 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186184354 1038 #edb/ref 17592186404244 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186198366 1038 #edb/ref 17592186404162 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186198366 1038 #edb/ref 17592186404169 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186404120 1068 #edb/ref 17592186404121 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186404120 1069 "q-80496" 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186404120 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186404120 1071 "Find matrices $P$ and $D$ such that $PD{P}^{-1}=B,$ where $D$ is a diagonal matrix and $B=[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 3 \\\\ -6 & 4\\end{aligned}].$" 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186404120 1072 #uuid "f53e1d4c-a53d-5c3e-8ae8-0e080a8e331f" 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186404120 1074 "We apply the diagonalization algorithm.\n\n**Step 1.** We need to find the eigenvalues of the matrix $B$ using its characteristic equation $det(B-\\lambda I)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}-5-\\lambda  & 3 \\\\ -6 & 4-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-5-\\lambda )(4-\\lambda )-3\\cdot (-6) & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}+\\lambda -2 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -1)(\\lambda +2) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the eigenvalues of $B$ are ${\\lambda }_{1}=1$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=-2.$ \n\n**Step 2.** Now, we need to find an eigenvector basis of $B.$\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{1}=1,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B-I & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 3 \\\\ -6 & 4\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 3 \\\\ -6 & 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have a system of linear equations with the augmented matrix $M$ which we reduce to its row echelon form using Gaussian elimination, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 3 & 0 \\\\ -6 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix above has one pivot column (the $1$st one). Thus, ${x}_{2}$ is a free variable. From the first equation, we obtain ${x}_{1}=\\frac{1}{2}{x}_{2}.$  Hence, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nSetting ${x}_{2}=2,$ we get the eigenvector ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{2}=-2,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B-(-2)I & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 3 \\\\ -6 & 4\\end{aligned}]-(-2)[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 3 \\\\ -6 & 6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have a system of linear equations with the augmented matrix $M$ which we reduce to its row echelon form using Gaussian elimination, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 3 & 0 \\\\ -6 & 6 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & ={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix above has one pivot column (the $1$st one). Thus, ${x}_{2}$ is a free variable. From the first equation, we obtain ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}.$ Hence, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nSetting ${x}_{2}=1,$ we get the eigenvector ${v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\n**Step 3.** We construct the diagonal matrix $D$ and the invertible matrix $P$ as follows:\n\n$$\nD=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}],\\,P=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186404121 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404122 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186404121 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404123 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186404121 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404124 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186404121 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404125 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186404121 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404126 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186404121 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186404121 1077 "selection" 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186404121 1079 #edb/ref 17592186404126 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186404121 1080 #uuid "5324a7ce-971d-53cb-b107-19a127a08e1f" 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186404122 1081 "$D=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]$ and\n$P=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]$" 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186404122 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186404122 1084 #uuid "20692b0c-ecf3-5857-b371-5e00dd088456" 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186404123 1081 "$B$ is not diagonalizable" 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186404123 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186404123 1084 #uuid "8297858c-6a75-5e90-8004-887fd5f4fe6e" 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186404124 1081 "$D=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]$ and\n$P=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{aligned}]$" 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186404124 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186404124 1084 #uuid "21bdb776-d042-5bc3-8def-4d142fb67170" 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186404125 1081 "$D=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]$ and\n$P=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}]$" 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186404125 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186404125 1084 #uuid "9a56eb51-adbb-529e-b66c-37695fb34a1f" 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186404126 1081 "$D=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]$ and\n$P=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]$" 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186404126 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186404126 1084 #uuid "3093f458-0d1e-55d2-af6e-2473cd7616a9" 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186404127 1068 #edb/ref 17592186404128 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186404127 1069 "q-80766" 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186404127 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186404127 1071 "Suppose that the function $f(x,y)$ and all of its first and second-order partial derivatives are continuous on an open set $U.$ Find the values of $a$ and $b$, if \n\n$$\n{f}_{x}(x,y)=y(1+x){e}^{x}+ax{y}^{3}+3{x}^{2},\\,{f}_{y}(x,y)=bx{e}^{x}-3{x}^{2}{y}^{2}.\n$$" 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186404127 1072 #uuid "f63374b4-82d5-5092-bcef-8ec87e149ab1" 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186404127 1074 "First, we find the mixed partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xy}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({f}_{x}(x,y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y(1+x){e}^{x}+ax{y}^{3}+3{x}^{2}) \\\\  & =(1+x){e}^{x}+3ax{y}^{2}+0 \\\\  & =(1+x){e}^{x}+3ax{y}^{2} \\\\ {f}_{yx}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({f}_{y}(x,y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(bx{e}^{x}-3{x}^{2}{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =b(1+x){e}^{x}-6x{y}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the function and its first and second-order partial derivatives are continuous on an open set $U,$ the mixed partial derivatives must be equal. Hence, we have the identity\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(1+x){e}^{x}+3ax{y}^{2}=b(1+x){e}^{x}-6x{y}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $(1+x){e}^{x}$ and $x{y}^{2},$ respectively, we see that $b=1$ and $a=-2.$" 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186404128 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404129 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186404128 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404130 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186404128 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404131 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186404128 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404132 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186404128 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404133 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186404128 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186404128 1077 "selection" 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186404128 1079 #edb/ref 17592186404133 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186404128 1080 #uuid "aa7f024f-dcae-5a46-aab4-36686da92a80" 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186404129 1081 "$a=1$, $b=2$" 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186404129 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186404129 1084 #uuid "37daf35b-b051-5de5-be26-c9ede321ab36" 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186404130 1081 "$a=-1$, $b=2$" 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186404130 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186404130 1084 #uuid "4eb42258-31a2-56c5-aa5a-940f6339e1ef" 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186404131 1081 "$a=2$, $b=e$" 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186404131 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186404131 1084 #uuid "92a398de-810f-54f4-a742-9f17711093b8" 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186404132 1081 "$a=-e$, $b=2$" 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186404132 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186404132 1084 #uuid "36f61f3a-a59d-517f-b778-17ee028f7808" 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186404133 1081 "$a=-2$, $b=1$" 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186404133 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186404133 1084 #uuid "7d026b63-b9dd-5d7f-972a-f02973c06d1d" 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186404134 1068 #edb/ref 17592186404135 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186404134 1069 "q-80825" 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186404134 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186404134 1071 "Determine all real eigenvalues $\\lambda $ of the matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -1\\end{aligned}].$" 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186404134 1072 #uuid "ba3b9cc6-841d-5636-9777-0bc1e8c24e7f" 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186404134 1074 "First, we find the matrix $\\,A-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nA-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}-1-\\lambda  & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2-\\lambda  & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe characteristic equation is given by $det(A-\\lambda I)=0.$ \n\nExpanding the determinant across the $1$st row, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}-1-\\lambda  & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2-\\lambda  & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-1-\\lambda )|\\begin{aligned}2-\\lambda  & 1 \\\\ 3 & -1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}|-1|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-{\\lambda }^{3}+6\\lambda +5)-(-1-\\lambda ) & =0 \\\\ -{\\lambda }^{3}+7\\lambda +6 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{3}-7\\lambda -6 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we need to solve this equation. We find the first root by testing some values. According to the rational zeros theorem, a list of good first guesses consists of all divisors of $6:$ \n\n$$\n\\pm 1,\\pm 2,\\pm 3,\\pm 6\n$$\n\n- Let's pick $x=1.$ Substituting to the characteristic equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(1)^{3}-7(1)-6 & =-12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $\\lambda =1$ is not a root of the equation.\n\n- Let's pick $x=-1.$ Substituting to the characteristic equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-1)^{3}-7(-1)-6 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $\\lambda =-1$ is a root of the equation.\n\nSo, we can factor $(\\lambda +1)$ out of ${\\lambda }^{3}-7\\lambda -6$ using synthetic division:\n\n| $-1$ | $1$ | $0$ | $-7$ | $-6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $↓$ | $-1$ | $1$ | $6$ |\n|  | $1$ | $-1$ | $-6$ | $0$ |\n\nSo, we obtain the following factorization:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\lambda +1)({\\lambda }^{2}-\\lambda -6) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +1)(\\lambda +2)(\\lambda -3) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are ${\\lambda }_{1}=-1,$ $\\,{\\lambda }_{2}=-2,\\,$ and $\\,{\\lambda }_{3}=3.$" 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186404135 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404136 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186404135 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404137 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186404135 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404138 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186404135 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404139 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186404135 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404140 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186404135 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186404135 1077 "selection" 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186404135 1079 #edb/ref 17592186404139 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186404135 1080 #uuid "135ac5a3-acd1-57d7-85af-ac59d7bb8214" 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186404136 1081 "\\lambda \\in {1,-6}" 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186404136 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533495 1759218604558