"The cup is red" 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186404235 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186404235 1084 #uuid "8d0f91ed-949b-5609-8a80-2ea003d3abbd" 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186404236 1081 "The cup is new or red" 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186404236 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186404236 1084 #uuid "6c4804d0-20da-5a86-b01a-abf2739587c3" 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186404237 1068 #edb/ref 17592186404238 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186404237 1069 "q-8306" 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186404237 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186404237 1071 "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=2yx+y{x}^{2}$ that satisfies $y(1)=1.$" 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186404237 1072 #uuid "177e97c5-b0fe-5fdf-abe1-80b42d3faf53" 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186404237 1074 "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2yx+y{x}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =y(2x+{x}^{2}) \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2x+{x}^{2} \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (2x+{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =2\\int x\\,\\text{d}x+\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & ={x}^{2}+\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the natural logarithm to both sides, we find the general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|} & ={e}^{{x}^{2}+{x}^{3}/3+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{{x}^{2}+{x}^{3}/3+C} \\\\ y & =\\pm {e}^{{x}^{2}+{x}^{3}/3+C} \\\\ y & =K{e}^{{x}^{2}+{x}^{3}/3},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K=\\pm {e}^{C}$ is an arbitrary constant. \n\nWe now apply the initial condition $y(1)=1$ to find $K:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(1) & =1 \\\\ K{e}^{{1}^{2}+{1}^{3}/3} & =1 \\\\ K{e}^{4/3} & =1 \\\\ K & ={e}^{-4/3}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus the particular solution of $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=2yx+y{x}^{2}$ that satisfies the condition $y(1)=1$ is\n\n$$\ny={e}^{-4/3}\\cdot {e}^{{x}^{2}+{x}^{3}/3}={e}^{({x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}-4)/3}\\,.\n$$" 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186404238 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404239 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186404238 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404240 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186404238 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404241 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186404238 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404242 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186404238 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404243 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186404238 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186404238 1077 "selection" 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186404238 1079 #edb/ref 17592186404243 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186404238 1080 #uuid "5399864b-fdb6-560a-bb1c-eadfa2e8485b" 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186404239 1081 "y={e}^{3{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}-1}" 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186404239 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186404239 1084 #uuid "aa22294c-97df-59d3-a2ef-bb723379bd93" 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186404240 1081 "y={e}^{({x}^{3}+{x}^{2}-2)/3}" 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186404240 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186404240 1084 #uuid "05c76659-9ee2-5ea1-9921-4c61064bc47c" 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186404241 1081 "y={e}^{(2{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}-1)/3}" 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186404241 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186404241 1084 #uuid "d957c339-7d86-5b49-bfb4-f34772448576" 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186404242 1081 "y={e}^{{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}-5}" 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186404242 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186404242 1084 #uuid "59acccda-8ad0-5671-8d3b-1eba77285637" 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186404243 1081 "y={e}^{({x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}-4)/3}" 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186404243 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186404243 1084 #uuid "08886f8e-1110-502c-b6b0-62359e9dd0d0" 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186404244 1068 #edb/ref 17592186404245 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186404244 1069 "q-83217" 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186404244 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186404244 1071 "Use the first two non-zero terms of the Taylor expansion of ${x}^{-1/2}$ about $x=9$ to approximate the value of ${8}^{-1/2}.$" 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186404244 1072 #uuid "f750b509-3c63-5fc0-8993-9bde234b6a4e" 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186404244 1074 "We use Taylor's formula in the form\n\n$$\nf(x)=f(a)+{f}^{′}(a)(x-a)+\\frac{{f}^{″}(a)}{2!}(x-a)^{2}+⋯,\n$$\n\nwith $a=9.$ \n\nCalculating the necessary derivatives, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & ={x}^{-1/2} \\\\ f(9) & ={9}^{-1/2}=\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & =-\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{-3/2} \\\\ {f}^{′}(9) & =-\\frac{1}{2}(9)^{-3/2}=-\\frac{1}{2\\cdot 27}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the Taylor series is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{-1/2} & =\\frac{1}{3}-\\frac{1}{2\\cdot 27}(x-9)+⋯ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}-\\frac{x-9}{54}+⋯.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute $x=8$ into the above to approximate ${8}^{-1/2}.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{8}^{-1/2} & ≈\\frac{1}{3}-\\frac{8-9}{54} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}+\\frac{1}{54} \\\\  & =\\frac{19}{54}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [17592186404245 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404246 13194139533495 17592186045585 true] [1759218640424